@@ -72,6 +72,16 @@ instrumentation, `e(sample)`, optional residual/absorbed/saved-FE outputs, and
 the receipt. Every N/K/K² value and output position is checked before stores.
 SPI calls stay on the Stata thread.
 
+The optional OLS request field `output_fill_missing` accepts only `0` or `1`
+and defaults to `0`. At `1`, native publication writes canonical Stata missing
+values to every excluded row of each requested numeric observation output,
+including saved channels. The ado adapter requests this behavior before using
+`st_addvar(..., 1)` for private output tempvars. An older plugin rejects the
+unknown field before reading observations; older callers can keep their
+missing-initialized shadows with the default. The sample marker retains its
+existing initialization. Uninitialized tempvars are never read or publicly
+renamed before successful complete publication, and every failure discards them.
+
 SPI has no physical rollback, so logical completion is receipt based. The
 `COMPLETE` cell is the final native operation; no allocation, polling,
 display, computation, or store follows it. The ado transaction validates the
